From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] cocoa: guest sizes that fit Omarchy's scale presets

What: in macOS full screen the guest gets up to 6 points fewer rows than
the area below the menu bar or the notch, as many as make Omarchy's scale
presets fit (ui/omacvm-clean-size.h). The window still fills the area
(Omanotch looks for a full-screen window down to the bottom edge); the
guest is drawn at its top, pixel for pixel (layer gravity top), the rows
left over black at the bottom, and the pointer there is on the guest's
last row. Without the IOSurface layer (OMACVM_GL_PRESENT=layer) the window
is fitted to the guest at the top instead. A window's content goes in 20
point steps (resizing, zoom, the first size), so the presets fit there
too. QEMU's log says the size ("omacvm: full screen: guest ...", on
change). The display layout the guest gets has the guest's rows only.

Why: Hyprland takes a scale only when the output divides into whole
logical pixels by it, and Omarchy's scale panel rounds its presets up to
those. The MacBook Air's area below the notch is 2940x1846 pixels: only 1x
and 2x fit, the panel offered nothing in between (user: "the macbook air
is missing scaling like 1.6 and 1.3 as an option"). At 2940x1840 (3 points
of black at the bottom) it offers 1, 1.25, 1.67, 2, 3.33 and 4. A 14-inch
MacBook Pro gets 3024x1888 (1.33, 1.6), a 16-inch keeps 3456x2160. A window
on 20 point steps always fits 1.25, 1.6 and 2 at 2x. The old rule (even
sizes at 2x) stays the floor.

Upstream: not applicable (Omarchy's presets).
Test: Tests/display/test-clean-size.sh (the picking); by hand on the
MacBook Air in full screen: Virtual-1 2940x1840, the scale panel offers
1.25, 1.67 and 2, the picture pixel for pixel, Omanotch's strip shown
(tracks: w2-scale-clean).
Applies after omacvm-cocoa-clean-size-logic.patch, last of the cocoa
patches.

